1. Scope

This proposed license covers only original material owned by Abacus in the
Abacus Studio plugin ("Abacus Material"). It does not cover third-party material,
client application code, client data, or independently created client work.
Third-party material remains governed by its applicable license; see
THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md. If these terms conflict with a third-party license for
that material, the third-party license controls. No broader rights are claimed
over upstream material merely because it appears in an adapted file.

2. Permitted use

Subject to an applicable agreement with Abacus and valid Studio authorization,
Abacus proposes to grant clients and their authorized personnel a non-exclusive,
non-transferable permission to install, execute, and make necessary local copies
of Abacus Material to develop, review, and maintain their authorized applications
through Abacus Studio and supported coding tools. Personnel must act for the
authorized client, not redistribute the plugin to unrelated parties.

Local modifications needed for that permitted use are allowed, but must not
bypass authorization, safety, or approval controls. Abacus is not obligated to
support modified copies. Client application output is not restricted by this
license solely because the plugin helped create it. Third-party code included
in an application remains subject to its own terms.

3. Restrictions on Abacus Material

Unless Abacus separately authorizes it in writing, recipients may not distribute,
sublicense, resell, rent, or offer Abacus Material as a hosted service; incorporate
it into a product competing with the Abacus Studio plugin or its managed
development workflows; or remove its copyright, attribution, or license notices.
These restrictions do not prohibit independently implementing general ideas,
methods, or functionality without copying protected Abacus Material.

Nothing limits rights under third-party licenses, mandatory law, or applicable
code-hosting terms, including viewing or forking where those terms permit it.
Public repository visibility does not itself grant additional commercial rights
to Abacus Material. No trademark rights are granted, and no endorsement by an
upstream author is implied.

4. Service and authorization boundaries

This license does not grant access to any application, repository, environment,
credential, or external service. Studio permissions and applicable service/client
agreements determine access. AI providers and coding tools have separate terms
and charges. Installing the plugin does not authorize publishing or production
changes. Revoking Studio access does not erase copies or rotate credentials
already present on a recipient's computer.

5. Termination

Abacus may terminate the proposed permission for a material breach that remains
uncured after written notice and a reasonable opportunity to cure, subject to any
controlling client agreement. On termination, recipients must stop using and
delete Abacus Material except copies required by law or a controlling agreement.
This does not require deleting client applications or independently licensed
